{"name":"Chardonnay","hex":"#efe8bc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Chardonnay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A green-skinned grape variety used to make a white wine.","A variety of wine made from this grape."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Chardonnay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chardonnay","blocks":[{"text":"Chardonnay is a green-skinned grape variety used in the production of white wine. The variety originated in the Burgundy wine region of east-central France, but is now grown wherever wine is produced, from England to New Zealand. For new and developing wine regions, growing Chardonnay is seen as a 'rite of passage' and an easy entry into the international wine market."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Chardonnay.jpg/330px-Chardonnay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chardonnay","wikidata":"Q213332"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Bouilleaud_blanc.jpg/500px-Bouilleaud_blanc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Bouilleaud_blanc.jpg/1280px-Bouilleaud_blanc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Bouilleaud_blanc.jpg/500px-Bouilleaud_blanc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gouais blanc, one of the parent varieties of Chardonnay","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABouilleaud_blanc.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Chardonnay_grapes_close_up.jpg/500px-Chardonnay_grapes_close_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Chardonnay_grapes_close_up.jpg/500px-Chardonnay